## 📖 Project Explanation: TascaEats (Phase 1)

### The Objective
[cite_start]To build a robust monolithic backend using **Spring Boot (Java)** that connects three types of users: **Clients**, **Restaurant Admins**, and **Drivers**[cite: 16, 17, 30]. [cite_start]In this first phase, there is **no graphical interface**; all interaction happens via a **REST API** documented through **Swagger**[cite: 60, 61].

### Core Architecture & Tech Stack
* [cite_start]**Framework:** Spring Boot[cite: 56].
* [cite_start]**Data Layer:** JPA / Spring Data with a **Relational Database**[cite: 55, 56].
* [cite_start]**Model:** A "Rich Domain Model" using inheritance and composition for entities[cite: 58].
* [cite_start]**Environment:** The entire application must run within **Docker**[cite: 65, 105].
* [cite_start]**Authentication:** Simplified via **Mock** (any password works if the user exists)[cite: 40, 54].

### Key Business Rules to Implement
Your system must enforce logic beyond simple data entry, such as:
* [cite_start]**Orders:** Cannot cancel if already in preparation; cannot order from closed restaurants[cite: 82, 84].
* [cite_start]**Inventory:** Cannot add out-of-stock products to an order[cite: 85].
* [cite_start]**Logistics:** Drivers cannot be assigned if they are unavailable[cite: 86].
* [cite_start]**Menu Management:** Products in old orders cannot be deleted (use "soft-delete")[cite: 83].


