## 🛠 Step-by-Step To-Do List

### Phase 1.1: Setup & Design (Week 1)
1.  [cite_start]**[ ] Fork & Permissions:** Fork the [official repository](https://git.alunos.di.fc.ul.pt/css000/tascaeats)[cite: 69]. [cite_start]Add group members as **Maintainers** and the account `css000` as **Reporter**[cite: 70, 71].
2.  [cite_start]**[ ] Domain Modeling:** Before coding, draw your Domain Model (UML)[cite: 124, 125]. [cite_start]Identify entities: `User` (and subclasses), `Restaurant`, `Product`, `Order`, `Payment`, and `Delivery`[cite: 19, 22, 23, 26, 27, 29].
3.  [cite_start]**[ ] Project Structure:** Initialize the Spring Boot project with dependencies (Web, Data JPA, Validation, H2/PostgreSQL, Lombok)[cite: 56, 59].

### Phase 1.2: The Domain & Data Layer (Week 2)
1.  [cite_start]**[ ] Implement Entities:** Create Java classes with JPA annotations[cite: 131]. [cite_start]Use `@Inheritance` for the different User roles[cite: 58, 132].
2.  [cite_start]**[ ] Persistence:** Create Spring Data Repositories for all entities[cite: 56].
3.  [cite_start]**[ ] Mock Auth:** Implement a service that validates users but accepts any password[cite: 40].

### Phase 1.3: Business Logic & API (Week 3)
1.  [cite_start]**[ ] Services Layer:** Implement the logic for Use Cases A through L (Login, User CRUD, Restaurant management, Ordering, etc.) [cite: 40-51].
2.  [cite_start]**[ ] Business Rules:** Code the specific constraints (e.g., checking if a restaurant is open before accepting an order)[cite: 80, 81].
3.  [cite_start]**[ ] REST Controllers:** Create endpoints for all Use Cases[cite: 73]. [cite_start]Ensure they use correct HTTP verbs and status codes[cite: 119].
4.  [cite_start]**[ ] DTOs:** Use Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) to expose only necessary data through the API[cite: 59].

### Phase 1.4: Infrastructure & Testing (Week 4)
1.  [cite_start]**[ ] Dockerization:** Create a `docker-compose.yml` that launches both the app and the database[cite: 98, 105].
2.  **[ ] Testing:** Write Unit and Integration tests. [cite_start]Aim for **80% coverage**[cite: 135, 136].
3.  [cite_start]**[ ] Query Validation:** Ensure your DB can answer business questions (e.g., "Which restaurant has the most sales?") [cite: 89-95].

### Phase 1.5: Final Delivery (Before April 10th)
1.  **[ ] Record Demonstration Videos:** Show the API working via Swagger. [cite_start]Must show JSON requests, responses, and the resulting changes in the database[cite: 74, 75].
2.  [cite_start]**[ ] Update README:** Include team identification and links to your videos[cite: 72, 99].
3.  [cite_start]**[ ] Git Tagging:** Create the `fase1` tag and push it to the server[cite: 97, 100, 101].

